  "raw": {
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Future-Student-Communications-Coordinator_R31353-2": {
      "title": "Future Student Communications Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nFuture Student Communications Coordinator Fixed Term - Full-Time | Sydney – Surry Hills | Face-to-Face / Hybrid Who We Are At Torrens University Australia, we believe education should connect people with opportunity and prepare them for real life. Our Future Students team plays an important role in helping prospective students move from initial enquiry through to application and enrolment. Behind that journey sits a sophisticated communications and marketing automation environment that ensures students receive the right information at the right time. We’re looking for a Future Student Communications Coordinator to join the team and help manage the operational and technical side of those communications. What’s the Job? This is a hands-on role sitting at the intersection of marketing automation, communications and technology . You’ll work within Salesforce Marketing Cloud to build, code, test and deliver communications across the future student journey — from first enquiry and event registration through to application and enrolment. You’ll work closely with Future Students, Marketing and Technology teams to transform campaign briefs into reliable, targeted and engaging communications. This role is particularly suited to someone who enjoys the technical side of marketing: building HTML emails, working with audience data, troubleshooting rendering issues, creating automation and using Salesforce Marketing Cloud to deliver personalised journeys at scale. Key Points About This Role Build & Deliver Email Campaigns   Create, code, test and deploy responsive EDMs and automated communications across multiple brands and future student journeys. Salesforce Marketing Cloud Operations   Work hands-on across Journey Builder, Email Studio, Mobile Studio and Automation Studio to manage campaigns, journeys and automation. Audience Data & Segmentation   Use SQL, data extensions and segmentation logic to identify the right audiences and ensure communications reach the right people. Customer Journey Automation   Build and maintain automated communications from enquiry through application, events and enrolment, supporting conversion across the student journey. Troubleshooting & Continuous Improvement   Identify rendering, coding or automation issues, solve problems quickly and continuously improve campaign performance and processes. Strategic Campaign Insight   Actively use reporting, analysis and insight to develop and optimise campaigns. Content & Design Optimisation   Recommend content and design improvements, grounded in email marketing best practice, to optimise campaign performance. Marketing Automation Advice   Provide strategic and tactical advice related to marketing automation technology and best practice. Who You Are You’re comfortable combining technical skills with marketing communications and enjoy turning briefs into working campaigns. You don’t need to know every answer immediately, but you’re resourceful, curious and confident researching solutions when something unfamiliar comes up. You’ll bring: Hands-On Email Coding Skills   Strong HTML experience for responsive email templates, including the ability to diagnose and resolve rendering issues across different email clients and devices. Salesforce Marketing Cloud Experience   Practical experience administering and configuring Salesforce Marketing Cloud and building communications within the platform. SQL & AMPscript Capability   Strong SQL skills for segmentation, data extensions and audience queries, plus AMPscript capability for dynamic content and personalisation. Marketing Automation Understanding   Experience creating customer journeys, triggered communications, nurturing programs and campaign automation. Strong Organisation & Communication   You can manage competing priorities, work to deadlines and communicate confidently with Marketing, Future Students, Technology and other stakeholders. Experience with CSS, front-end development, media queries, dark-mode coding or email-client-specific coding techniques will be highly regarded. Salesforce Marketing Cloud Email Specialist certification and Salesforce Lightning experience are also advantageous. Why Join Us? This is an opportunity to work in a role where technology and communication directly influence the future student experience. You’ll help manage communications across multiple brands and audiences, supporting prospective students from their first interaction with us through to enrolment. You’ll also work in a collaborative and multicultural team where people share ideas, solve problems together and are encouraged to keep learning. The environment is fast-moving, and priorities can sometimes change quickly. We’re looking for someone who enjoys that pace, can respond calmly when urgent communications arise and is comfortable finding solutions rather than waiting for them. What We Offer Sydney-based role in Surry Hills Face-to-face and hybrid ways of working Hands-on exposure to Salesforce Marketing Cloud and marketing automation Opportunity to work across multiple brands, audiences and customer journeys Collaborative work across Future Students, Marketing and Technology Professional development and opportunities to build your technical marketing capability Exposure to events, campaigns and broader student recruitment activity From time to time, you may be required to support university events such as Open Days, including occasional weekend or after-hours activity. Hiring Process We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog . We’d love to hear from you. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Senior-Advisor-Learning---Development_R31310": {
      "title": "Senior Advisor Learning & Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.  Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.  What’s the job?   As the Senior Learning and Development Advisor , you will support the design, coordination and delivery of learning an development initiatives across Torrens Global Education. Working with the Head of Talent and HR colleagues, you will help build a culture of continuous learning, growth and knowledge sharing across the organisation.  You will coordinate training programs and learning activities, facilitate engaging virtual sessions, create practical learning resources and support employees in accessing development opportunities. You will also work with stakeholders to maintain learning content, coordinate LMS activities and help evaluate the effectiveness of learning initiatives. You will regularly collaborate with our parent company, Strategic Education, Inc. (SEI), on the rollout of joint initiatives across Torrens University Australia.   The role is suited to an organised and engaging learning professional who can manage multiple priorities, communicate confidently with diverse stakeholders and turn business needs into accessible, high-quality learning experiences.  Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   Work with the HR team to identify learning needs and develop suitable programs, using existing tools and initiatives while creating new learning assets where required.  Organise and schedule training sessions, workshops and seminars, including communications, venue or virtual arrangements, equipment and participant registration.  Support and independently facilitate engaging training sessions and workshops, predominantly in virtual environments, and prepare other facilitators where required.  Develop and update presentations, handouts, multimedia content and other resources to support effective learning experiences.  Work with HRIS specialists to manage learning activity in the LMS. Exciting projects you will be working on in 2027   Support the development and implementation of AI literacy and AI-related capability programs across the organisation.  Coordinate and support the rollout of the Know Where You Stand (Performance and Development) Cycle for 2027.  Drive and administer compliance training programs.  Support the rollout of a bespoke leadership skills model in the latter part of 2027.  Drive “SEED” internal  Mentoring Program across ANZ, now entering its fourth year.  Who you are   A learning and development professional with experience coordinating and delivering training or employee development initiatives.  A holder of a bachelor-level qualification, preferably in psychology, human resources or a related discipline; a Certificate IV in Training and Assessment is advantageous.  Experienced facilitating training for large groups, particularly in online or virtual environments.  Experienced in program coordination or administration with a strong customer service and stakeholder support focus.  Highly proficient with technology, including Microsoft Office, SharePoint, PowerPoint and Teams, with advanced virtual meeting skills using platforms such as Teams or Zoom.  Experienced using a learning management system; Workday LMS experience is preferred.  A confident communicator and presenter who can collaborate effectively with diverse people across ANZ and US teams.  Highly organised, self-directed and able to manage multiple tasks, projects or campaigns concurrently.  Passionate about continuous learning and growth, with exposure to psychometric tools such as Hogan, Gallup or HBDI considered advantageous.  To read more about the role please click here .  This is a full-time, permanent position offering hybrid flexibility, with the opportunity to work from home and from one of our campuses. Preferred location Sydney or Melbourne.   Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.  We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.  What we offer :  We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:  Study free in a course/degree related to your position  Access to internal opportunities - be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation  A purpose-driven workplace that values community, collaboration and innovation  Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.  We’d love to hear from you.  Job reference:  R31310 Applications for this role will close on 8th November If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Revenue-Operations-Manager_R31352-1": {
      "title": "Revenue Operations Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nRevenue Operations Manager Permanent Full-Time | Hybrid | Sydney preferred, other locations considered Who We Are At Torrens University Australia, we do things differently. We believe education should connect people with opportunity and prepare them for real life. As part of Torrens Global Education Services, our Future Students & Growth team connects prospective students with study options that can transform their futures. Behind that work sits a complex commercial engine spanning sales, marketing, admissions, technology, data and student operations.  We’re now looking for our first dedicated Revenue Operations Manager to help us build the next generation of that engine. What’s the Job? This is not a traditional reporting or data analyst role.  As Revenue Operations Manager , you’ll own the systems, data, processes, forecasting and commercial insight underpinning student recruitment and revenue performance across our education portfolio.  You’ll establish a trusted source of truth across the Future Students & Growth function, connecting the entire journey from enquiry through application, enrolment and census to revenue.  You’ll combine commercial thinking, sales operations expertise and technical capability to help leaders understand not only what is happening, but why it is happening, what is likely to happen next, and what we should do about it.  As our first dedicated RevOps hire, you’ll have a genuine opportunity to build the function from the ground up.  Key Points About This Role   Revenue Forecasting & Commercial Modelling   Build forecasting models across acquisition, study load, attrition, retention and census-surviving revenue to improve predictability and commercial decision-making.  Performance Insight & Incentives   Own reporting across productivity, conversion, pipeline, targets and incentives, turning complex performance data into clear actions for leaders and teams.  Funnel & Channel Economics   Understand where value is created or lost across the enquiry-to-census funnel and analyse conversion, velocity, attribution, agents and channel return.  CRM, Systems & Data Governance   Own and optimise the Future Students technology environment, including Salesforce, integrations, automation, data quality and reliable metric definitions.  Process Improvement & Revenue Enablement   Design better processes, remove manual friction and establish the operating rhythm, documentation and systems that help sales teams perform at their best.  Who You Are   You are commercially curious, technically capable and naturally action-oriented.  You don’t just produce reports—you understand how sales functions operate, recognise the commercial story behind the numbers and can translate insight into action.  You’ll bring:  Revenue or Sales Operations Experience   At least five years’ experience across Revenue Operations, Sales Operations, Marketing Operations, commercial analytics or a comparable systems and insight environment.  Strong Commercial & Sales Acumen   A strong understanding of sales funnels, conversion, pipeline, forecasting and performance measures, with the ability to connect activity to commercial outcomes.  CRM & Automation Expertise   Hands-on ownership of CRM platforms, ideally Salesforce, including configuration, automation, reporting and administration. Salesforce certification is highly regarded.  Advanced Analytics Capability   Advanced Excel skills and strong Power BI, Tableau or equivalent visualisation capability. SQL experience is strongly preferred.  Builder Mentality   You’re comfortable stepping into ambiguity, setting priorities and building something from the ground up. You move quickly, solve problems and enjoy operating in a high-performing environment.  You’ll also be confident presenting insights to senior and non-technical audiences, influencing stakeholders without formal authority and working with sensitive performance and remuneration information with discretion.  A tertiary qualification in Business, Commerce, Analytics, Information Systems or a related discipline—or equivalent practical experience—is expected.  Experience within higher education is not essential . We are particularly interested in candidates who bring strong commercial Revenue Operations or Sales Operations capability from other industries.  Experience with commission structures, multi-period revenue forecasting, complex sales channels or regulated environments will be highly regarded.  Why Join Us?   This is a rare opportunity to join a function at the beginning of its Revenue Operations journey.  Rather than inheriting a mature operating model, you’ll have the opportunity to shape it.  You’ll work closely with senior leaders across Future Students & Growth, Marketing, Admissions, Finance, Technology, Data & Analytics, People & Culture and Student Administration to create better visibility, stronger forecasting and more effective commercial decision-making.  The environment is fast-moving and ambitious. Priorities can change quickly, and we value people who can understand what matters, act decisively and deliver.  If you enjoy solving complex commercial problems, working across systems and data, and seeing your insights directly influence business performance, this role offers considerable scope to make an impact.  What We Offer   A permanent, full-time opportunity within Torrens University Australia  Hybrid and flexible ways of working  The opportunity to establish and shape a new Revenue Operations capability  Exposure to senior leaders and commercially significant strategic projects  A collaborative environment where experimentation, continuous improvement and new ways of working are encouraged  Professional development and opportunities to grow across Torrens Global Education Services  Sydney is the preferred location for this role; however, we are open to considering an outstanding candidate based in another suitable location.   Occasional interstate travel may be required.  Hiring Process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support.  We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We’d love to hear from you. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Future-Student-Advisor---Health_R31351-1": {
      "title": "Future Student Advisor – Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nFuture Student Advisor – Health   Sydney or Melbourne Preferred | 2 Opportunities | Permanent Full-Time Are you a confident communicator who enjoys building relationships, achieving targets and helping students shape their future? Torrens University Australia is looking for two motivated and results-driven Future Student Advisors – Health to join our Student Recruitment team. In this sales-focused role, you'll connect with prospective students, understand their study aspirations and guide them through their journey from initial enquiry to enrolment. You'll manage student enquiries, provide course and admissions information, and help prospective students make informed decisions about their education. This opportunity is ideal for someone who enjoys consultative sales, student engagement and making a genuine difference in people's lives. What's the Role?   As a Future Student Advisor – Health , you'll support prospective students throughout the admissions and enrolment process, ensuring an exceptional student experience. You'll manage enquiries, assess applications against published entry criteria, nurture student leads and contribute to recruitment and enrolment targets. Working closely with admissions, academic and recruitment teams, you'll help students navigate their education options while maintaining accurate records and compliant admissions processes. Key Points About This Role Student Engagement: Build meaningful relationships with prospective students and provide personalised course and enrolment guidance. Lead Generation & Conversion: Manage student enquiries, nurture leads and achieve recruitment and enrolment targets. Admissions Support: Review applications against entry criteria and refer exceptions to Program Managers. CRM & Pipeline Management: Maintain accurate Salesforce records, manage timely follow-ups and monitor recruitment performance. Team Collaboration: Work with admissions, academic and recruitment teams to support student enrolments and recruitment activities. To read more about the role, please click here . Who You Are   You're a proactive, results-driven professional who enjoys connecting with people and achieving meaningful outcomes. You'll bring: Experience in sales, student recruitment, admissions or another target-driven environment. Strong communication, customer service and relationship-building skills. A proven ability to manage enquiries, follow up leads and achieve conversion targets. Confidence using Salesforce or similar CRM systems, with intermediate to advanced Microsoft Word and Excel skills. Excellent organisation, attention to detail and the ability to work independently. Higher Education or VET admissions experience is advantageous, and a relevant tertiary qualification is desirable. Why Join Us?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we're committed to transforming lives through education and helping students access opportunities that shape their future. As a Future Student Advisor – Health, you'll join a collaborative, purpose-led team with opportunities for professional development and career growth. We are an equal opportunity employer committed to inclusion and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and people from all backgrounds. What We Offer   Study opportunities: Free study in eligible courses related to your role.  Purpose-led culture: Be part of a B Corp certified university.  Career growth: Access learning and internal development opportunities.  Meaningful work: Help students take the next step towards their future.    Hiring Process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support.  We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We'd love to hear from you.     Job reference: R31351 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 20th November. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with any updates about your application.  If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/QLD-Remote/Future-Student-Advisor---Schools_R31350-1": {
      "title": "Future Student Advisor - Schools",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nFuture Student Advisor – Schools Remote QLD: Cairns or Townsville | Permanent Full-Time   Are you a confident relationship builder who enjoys getting out into the community, creating opportunities and turning conversations into meaningful outcomes?  Torrens University Australia is looking for a motivated and results-driven Future Student Advisor – Schools to join our Student Recruitment team in North Queensland.  This is a remote-based, field-focused sales role where you'll build strong relationships with schools, connect with future students and help them discover education pathways that align with their aspirations.  You'll engage with career advisers, teachers, school leaders, students and families, generating quality leads and supporting prospective students through their journey from initial interest to enrolment.   This opportunity is ideal for someone who enjoys relationship-led sales, school visits, presentations, events and making a genuine difference in students' lives.  What's the role?   As a Future Student Advisor – Schools , you'll represent Torrens University Australia across schools, career expos, information sessions and student engagement activities throughout your assigned North Queensland territory.  You'll focus on developing and strengthening school relationships, identifying recruitment opportunities, generating prospective student leads and contributing to enrolment outcomes across our course offerings.  While based remotely in Cairns or Townsville, this is an active, outward-facing role that combines school engagement, relationship management, sales and student recruitment.  You'll have the autonomy to manage your territory, build your pipeline and create meaningful connections that help students take their next step towards higher education.  Key Points About This Role   Build School Relationships: Develop and maintain strong partnerships with career advisers, teachers, school leaders and key contacts across your assigned territory.  Drive Student Engagement: Represent Torrens University at school visits, career expos, information sessions and events, delivering engaging presentations about study pathways.  Generate Leads & Enrolments : Identify opportunities, nurture prospective students and convert enquiries into applications and enrolments while working towards recruitment targets.  Manage Your Sales Pipeline: Maintain accurate school, lead and student records in Salesforce, prioritise follow-ups and monitor recruitment activity to drive performance.  Collaborate for Success: Work closely with admissions, enrolments, marketing and student recruitment teams to create a seamless student experience and support recruitment activities.  To read more about the role, please click here .  Who You Are   You're a motivated, student-focused professional who enjoys connecting with people and achieving meaningful results. You combine a genuine interest in education with commercial awareness, strong communication skills and a proactive approach.   You’ll bring:  Experience in sales, business development, student recruitment, account management or another target-driven role.  Confidence building relationships with schools, stakeholders, students and families.  Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to engage and influence diverse audiences.  A proactive approach to generating leads, following up opportunities and achieving conversion targets.  Excellent organisation and time management skills, with the ability to work independently in a remote environment.  Experience using CRM systems, ideally Salesforce, alongside intermediate to advanced Microsoft Word and Excel skills.  Strong attention to detail when maintaining student records, managing applications and supporting admissions processes.  Resilience, initiative and a genuine passion for helping students achieve their education goals.  Higher Education or VET admissions experience is advantageous, and a relevant tertiary qualification is desirable.  Why Join Us?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA.  As a Certified B Corporation, we're committed to transforming lives through education and helping students access opportunities that shape their future.  As a Future Student Advisor team, you'll join a collaborative, purpose-led team with opportunities for professional development and career growth.  We are an equal opportunity employer committed to inclusion and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and people from all backgrounds.  What We Offer   Study opportunities: Free study in eligible courses related to your role.  Purpose-led culture: Be part of a B Corp certified university.  Career growth: Access learning and internal development opportunities.  Meaningful work: Help students take the next step towards their future.    Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support.  We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We'd love to hear from you.  Job reference: R31350 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 20th November. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with any updates about your application.    If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Senior-Future-Student-Advisor_R31346": {
      "title": "Senior Future Student Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nSenior Future Student Advisor – Health   Permanent Full-Time | Hybrid Flexibility | Adelaide Preferred Are you a high-performing sales professional who enjoys mentoring others, driving results and making a meaningful impact? Torrens University Australia is looking for an experienced Senior Future Student Advisor – Health to join our Student Recruitment team in Adelaide. In this senior sales role, you'll lead by example, achieve enrolment targets, coach fellow advisors and help improve team performance while supporting future students on their education journey. Who We Are   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we believe in the power of education to transform lives and create opportunities. We're a purpose-led university where collaboration, innovation and student success are at the heart of everything we do. What's the Job?   You'll drive student recruitment outcomes while supporting the Student Recruitment Manager as second-in-command. Combining your sales expertise with coaching and mentoring, you'll help strengthen team capability, improve conversion rates and deliver an exceptional student experience. This role will focus on the strategic vision of growth of our Health programs for the Adelaide market, with increasing investment. It is an exciting time to take part in connecting future students with the new offerings available. Key Points About This Role Drive Enrolment Results: Consistently achieve and exceed individual enrolment targets. Act growth strategy: Torrens is bringing a strong focus on Health to the Adelaide Market, you will bring this to life  Student Engagement: Build meaningful relationships with prospective students and provide personalised course and enrolment guidance. CRM & Pipeline Management: Maintain accurate Salesforce records, manage timely follow-ups and monitor recruitment performance. Support Team Leadership: Act as second-in-command to the Student Recruitment Manager and role-model best practices. Coach & Mentor: Support new advisors through call coaching, mentoring and performance guidance. To read more about the role, please click here . Who You Are   You're a confident, results-driven sales professional who enjoys sharing knowledge and helping others succeed.  You'll bring:  Proven Sales Performance: Demonstrated success meeting and exceeding targets, ideally in higher education.  Coaching & Mentoring: Previous experience training, mentoring and developing colleagues.  Relevant Experience: A minimum of three years' professional experience in a similar role.  Communication & Systems: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, sound Microsoft Excel knowledge and confidence learning new technologies.  Autonomy & Collaboration: Ability to work independently, contribute to team success and adapt to changing priorities.    Why Join Us?   Join a university committed to making education accessible and helping students achieve their goals.  You'll have the opportunity to share your expertise, develop others and contribute to a collaborative, high-performing recruitment team.  We are an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and people from all backgrounds.  What We Offer   Study opportunities: Eligible free study opportunities in courses related to your role.  Purpose-led culture: Be part of a B Corp certified university.  Career development: Access learning and internal growth opportunities.  Meaningful impact: Help develop future student advisors and support student success.  Hiring Process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support.  We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We'd love to hear from you.   Job reference: R31346 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 20th November. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with any updates about your application. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Senior-Application-Engineer---Salesforce_R31192-2": {
      "title": "Senior Application Engineer - Salesforce",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWho we are? At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do. About the role: We’re looking for a Senior Application Engineer - Salesforce to play a critical role in the development, implementation and maintenance of our Salesforce CRM and Marketing Cloud platforms within a complex, integrated environment. This role focuses on building and supporting integrations between Salesforce and our Student Management System, Banner, using Informatica, along with a range of other connected systems. You’ll bring strong Salesforce development experience, a solid understanding of CRM and marketing automation, and a hands-on approach to coding, configuration and troubleshooting. Working closely with teams across the organisation, you’ll help deliver practical, scalable and high-quality solutions that support business outcomes, improve user experience and strengthen the way our platforms operate. Key accountabilities (but not limited to): Salesforce development & customisation: Design, build and enhance Salesforce CRM and Marketing Cloud solutions using Apex, Lightning (Aura and LWC) and configuration best practice. System configuration & maintenance: Configure, maintain and continuously improve Salesforce environments to support business operations, system performance, reliability and user experience. Integrations & connected systems: Deliver and support robust integrations between Salesforce, Banner and other enterprise systems using REST and SOAP APIs, platform events, webhooks, middleware and integration platforms including Informatica. Marketing Cloud & AI enablement: Lead development and optimisation across Marketing Cloud, including Email Studio, Journey Builder, Automation Studio, Contact Builder, AMPscript and SQL, while staying informed about Agentforce, Einstein, Data Cloud and other AI capabilities. Hands-on technical leadership: Troubleshoot complex issues, perform root-cause analysis, provide production support and continuously improve performance, scalability, reliability, security and engineering quality across the Salesforce ecosystem. Quality assurance & engineering practices: Apply secure coding practices, peer review, unit testing, integration testing and Salesforce platform best practice to deliver high-quality, maintainable solutions with reduced defects. Release & environment management: Support controlled Salesforce deployments across development, testing and production environments using GitLab, including validation, documentation, rollback planning and minimal disruption to business operations.   Collaboration & solution design: Work closely with IT, Marketing, Student Services, Product Owners, business analysts, QA, release and support teams to understand business needs, translate them into technical solutions and deliver outcomes that are fit-for-purpose and future-ready.   Documentation, training & strategic planning: Maintain accurate technical documentation, deliver training and knowledge sharing, and contribute to the IT roadmap, platform continuous improvement, technical debt reduction and engineering maturity. Who you are: You’re a senior Salesforce engineer who is deeply technical, analytical and hands-on by nature, with the communication skills to work confidently with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. You’ll bring: A tertiary qualification or formal training in IT, Computing Studies, Information Systems or a related discipline. At least five years of hands-on Salesforce development experience, preferably in an enterprise or higher education environment. Demonstrated experience with Apex, SOQL, Lightning Web Components, Flow, Visualforce, Aura, custom objects and fields, data modelling and Salesforce security. Experience with Salesforce Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud and Marketing Cloud, including Email Studio, Journey Builder, Automation Studio, Contact Builder, AMPscript and SQL. Proven experience designing and supporting Salesforce integrations using REST, SOAP, platform events, middleware and integration platforms such as Informatica. Knowledge of Salesforce authentication, sharing, profiles, permission sets, governor limits, performance considerations and secure integration patterns. Experience with CI/CD and release tools such as GitLab, Azure DevOps, Gearset, Copado or equivalent. Salesforce Platform Developer I certification, which is required. Platform Developer II, Administrator, Platform App Builder, Marketing Cloud or Architect certifications are desirable. Knowledge of Agentforce, Einstein, Salesforce AI capabilities or Data Cloud is desirable. Strong troubleshooting, analytical, communication and stakeholder-management skills, with experience working in Agile or similar delivery methodologies. Experience participating in code reviews, technical design reviews, testing, release planning and production support. Formal Salesforce certifications (Platform Developer, Marketing Cloud) are highly regarded, but your depth of hands-on capability and problem-solving mindset matter most.  This is a full-time, permanent position with hybrid flexibility to work from home and a campus near you. Preferred locations are Sydney and Melbourne.  To review the full job description please 'Click Here’ .   Why join us? Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, with 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and more than 2,000 staff. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer: We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from: Study free in a course or degree related to your position Access to internal opportunities – be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation A collaborative, purpose-driven working environment where your work can make a meaningful difference Hiring process: We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog. We’d love to hear from you. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Academic-Services-Compliance-and-Reporting-Specialist_R31277-2": {
      "title": "Academic Services Compliance and Reporting Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWho we are:   At Torrens University Australia , making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.    A progressive university, we ground our studies in industry. Expert academics bring their insights into the classroom, with a range of assessment types that aim to be authentic and informed by industry needs. Bridging the gap between study and work, our educators prepare students for career success and connect them with future employers. Building relevant skills, experience and networks from day one, students don’t just learn about their industry, they live it.    What’s the job?   The Academic Services Compliance and Reporting Specialist supports the Associate Registrar, Student Governance and Compliance, by coordinating compliance, risk, assurance, reporting and business improvement activities across Academic Administration Services and Student Experience. You will help maintain reliable governance information and evidence, support the implementation of regulatory and policy requirements, and provide reporting and analysis that assists risk management, assurance and service improvement. The role also provides delegated operational support for external complaints and National Student Ombudsman matters, escalating complex or high-risk issues to the Associate Registrar.    Principle accountabilities (but not limited to): Compliance, Risk and Assurance: manage compliance, risk and assurance activities, maintain registers and evidence repositories, conduct assurance reviews, and track corrective actions. Reporting, Data Quality and Performance: prepare quarterly reports, validate data, identify trends and anomalies, and maintain reporting documentation and evidence trails. External Complaints and National Student Ombudsman: coordinate complaints and investigations, prepare evidence-based responses, monitor deadlines, and track outcomes and remedial actions. Implementation and Business Improvement: coordinate compliance and improvement initiatives, including policies, processes, controls, milestones, dependencies, risks and stakeholder consultation. Student-Centred Insight and Responsible AI: analyse student feedback, complaints and service trends, and use approved digital and AI tools responsibly to support improvement and reporting. Who you are:   An experienced compliance, risk, assurance, reporting or business improvement professional who has worked in a complex or regulated environment, preferably higher education, vocational education or a comparable sector. Experienced in coordinating projects or improvement initiatives from planning through to implementation and follow-through. Confident maintaining risk registers, action plans, controls, evidence, reporting schedules and data-quality processes. Skilled in preparing reports, dashboards or briefing materials that identify trends, quantify activity and support sound decision-making. Experienced in coordinating sensitive complaints, regulatory investigations or National Student Ombudsman matters, including evidence collation, stakeholder coordination and deadline management. A clear and concise written communicator with strong analytical capability, attention to detail and confidence working with data, trends, metrics and quality checks. Able to exercise sound judgement, identify matters requiring escalation and follow issues through to resolution. Collaborative and student-centred, with the ability to build constructive relationships and coordinate contributions across multiple teams without direct authority. Digitally confident, including the responsible use of reporting tools, workflow systems and artificial intelligence with human oversight. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in business, education, law, governance, compliance, risk, quality, data, student administration or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant professional experience. Qualifications or professional development in compliance, risk, audit, quality assurance, project management, data analysis or business improvement are desirable. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent, full-time position. The preferred location for this role is at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney. Other campus locations may be considered (Brisbane, Melbourne, Adelaide).  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we are Australia's fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country's most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you will find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer: Study free in a course or degree related to your position. B Corp certified university - values driven and purpose led. Access to internal opportunities - be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation. A collaborative, student-focused environment where you can help shape the future of academic services.  Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31277 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 12 November 2026. Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Student-Complaints-Officer_R31112": {
      "title": "Student Complaints Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.    Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.    What’s the job?   As the Student Complaints Officer , you’ll support the Student Complaints Manager to manage and resolve a significant volume of student complaints and appeals, including matters relating to academic integrity and generative AI. You’ll help ensure each matter is handled fairly, consistently and transparently, while keeping students informed and maintaining accurate, auditable records.    You’ll investigate complaints and appeals, assess evidence, prepare clear case summaries and recommendations, and draft outcome correspondence in plain English. You’ll provide practical advice on the Student Complaints Policy and related procedures, work with academic and professional teams on complex matters, and contribute to improvements that strengthen confidence in the University’s complaint-handling processes.    Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   Triage new appeals, set priorities and maintain momentum across a high-volume caseload.  Gather and test evidence, liaise with relevant parties, verify policy application and assess appropriate remedies.  Prepare accurate reports, succinct case summaries, recommendations and plain-English outcome letters.  Keep complainants and appellants informed about processes, timelines and outcomes, de-escalating concerns where possible.  Identify and refer urgent welfare or safety risks through established pathways.  Apply policies and procedures consistently, ensuring procedural fairness, independence and the absence of conflicts of interest.  Meet acknowledgement and resolution timeframes, recording defensible reasons for any extensions.  Safeguard privacy and confidentiality and maintain accurate records in approved records management systems.  Provide specialist advice on appeals, including academic integrity breaches and generative AI use.  Work with the Student Complaints Manager, Policy and Academic Governance, Legal and relevant offices on complex or high-risk matters.  Contribute to complaint-handling resources, training, benchmarking and continuous improvement activities.  Build respectful relationships with students, academics and professional staff while delivering outstanding service.    Who you are:   An experienced complaints or case management professional with at least five years’ experience managing student complaints, preferably within a university or comparable education environment.  Confident handling appeals and complaints involving academic integrity issues, including the use of generative AI.  Highly organised and detail-focused, with the ability to manage a high-volume workload accurately and efficiently.  A clear and empathetic communicator who can write concise, well-reasoned correspondence for diverse audiences, including people who speak English as an additional language.  Knowledgeable in administrative policies, procedures, privacy, procedural fairness and records management.  Collaborative and resilient, with a student-service mentality and the judgement to balance people, compliance and organisational needs.  Technically capable, including strong skills in word processing, spreadsheets and enterprise records management systems.  An undergraduate-qualified professional, or someone with equivalent relevant experience.    To read more about the role please click here .  This is a full-time, permanent role that can be based at any of our four campuses. Offering hybrid flexibility to work from home or allocated campus days.    Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.    We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.    We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.    What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:  Study free in a course or degree related to your position  Access to internal opportunities – be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation  A values-driven and purpose-led working environment  Hiring process:   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.    If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.  We’d love to hear from you.    Job reference: R31112    Applications for this role will close on Friday 4 December.    Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.  If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Senior-Learning-Facilitator_R31377": {
      "title": "Senior Learning Facilitator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nSenior Lecturer, Exercise Science About Torrens University At Torrens University, we are committed to providing students with a transformative educational experience that combines academic excellence, industry relevance and personalised support. As Australia's fastest-growing university, we focus on preparing graduates for meaningful careers through innovative teaching, strong industry engagement and a student-centred approach to learning. We are seeking an experienced and passionate academic to join our Rehabilitation Sciences team as a a Senior Lecturer. This is an exciting opportunity to help shape and grow our Exercise Science pathway, delivering exceptional student experiences while contributing to the future development of our rehabilitation and allied health portfolio. This role will play a key part in preparing graduates for employment within the health, fitness and exercise sectors, while supporting clear progression pathways into further study and professional careers in rehabilitation sciences. The role combines teaching excellence, student success, subject leadership, academic administration and operational coordination within a growing area of strategic importance for the University. About the Role The Senior Lecturer is responsible for delivering high-quality teaching and learning outcomes across Exercise Science subjects and programs while supporting the effective day-to-day operation of this growing area within the Rehabilitation Sciences portfolio. This is a teaching-focused academic role that combines teaching excellence, student success, subject leadership, academic administration and operational coordination. Working closely with students, colleagues and industry stakeholders, you will create engaging and supportive learning experiences that help students achieve their educational and career goals. You will contribute to the ongoing growth of Exercise Science at Torrens University, supporting pathways that provide direct employment opportunities within the fitness industry and progression into broader rehabilitation and allied health disciplines. Day-to-day accountabilities: Key responsibilities are listed below and may change based on program needs and individual areas of skill and expertise: Teaching and Student Experience   Subject Leadership, Coordination and Operations   Curriculum Development and Academic Quality   Industry & Professional Engagement   Collaboration & Contribution This is a full-time ongoing position, primarily based at our Melbourne campus, with flexible working options.  Click here to read Job Description . Who you are You are a passionate educator who is committed to helping students succeed and who understands the importance of combining academic quality with practical career outcomes. You will bring: A postgraduate qualification in Exercise Science, Sport and Exercise Science, Strength and Conditioning, Exercise Physiology or a related discipline. Experience teaching within higher education, including both online and face-to-face delivery. Demonstrated ability to create engaging and student-centred learning experiences. Experience supporting student success, retention and progression. Experience coordinating subjects, academic operations or related educational activities. Strong organisational and administrative skills with the ability to manage competing priorities. Excellent communication, collaboration and stakeholder engagement skills. Strong disciplinary knowledge and the ability to connect theory with industry-relevant practice. A commitment to academic quality, continuous improvement and evidence-informed practice.  Why Join Torrens University? Help build a new generation of Exercise Science pathways that create direct employment opportunities in the fitness industry and progression opportunities into rehabilitation and allied health careers. Play a key role in shaping an emerging area within the Rehabilitation Sciences portfolio. Join a collaborative and supportive academic community committed to student success. Access professional development and career growth opportunities. Enjoy flexible working arrangements and hybrid delivery models. Study in a course or qualification related to your role. Contribute to innovative programs that create meaningful educational and career pathways for students. Our Culture Our people are collaborative, innovative and passionate about making a positive difference through education. At Torrens University, you will join a community that values excellence in teaching, continuous improvement, student success and meaningful industry engagement. We are committed to creating an inclusive workplace where diverse perspectives are welcomed and where employees are supported to grow, contribute and thrive. Please note, if you are successful in securing this role, you will be required to submit: Current Working with Children Check Certified copies of all your Academic qualifications Hiring process   We aim to make our recruitment process transparent, inclusive and supportive. If you have any accessibility requirements or need adjustments, please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. Start date: available for immediate start.  Application close: COB Sunday 29th November Job reference: R31377 If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/WA-Remote/Senior-Learning-Facilitator--Counselling---Psychotherapy-_R31370-1": {
      "title": "Senior Learning Facilitator (Counselling & Psychotherapy)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-11\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do. What’s the job?   As the Senior Learning Facilitator in Counselling & Psychotherapy , you will contribute to teaching, scholarship and, where agreed, research within the School of Health Sciences and Clinical Practice. You will prepare, deliver and assess subjects across online and on-campus learning environments, ensuring students are supported to achieve their learning outcomes and successfully progress through their studies. You will also contribute to course review, curriculum development, assessment innovation, validation, moderation and academic quality activities. Depending on your skills and experience, you may coordinate subjects or sites, lead academic projects, mentor academic staff and contribute to industry or professional practice engagement. The role is suited to an experienced academic or professional practitioner who can deliver engaging, student-centred learning and contribute to the continued development of Counselling & Psychotherapy education. Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to): Prepare and deliver engaging lectures, seminars, tutorials, workshops, forums and practical learning activities using innovative online and on-campus teaching practices. Develop, review and update teaching materials, assessment tools and learning resources, ensuring they support subject learning outcomes and quality requirements. Conduct student assessment, provide timely and constructive feedback, determine final results and participate in validation, moderation and course review activities. Monitor student engagement, attendance and progress, identify students at risk and work with relevant academic support teams to promote student success. Contribute to curriculum development, subject coordination, academic projects, mentoring and academic leadership activities as agreed with the Course Lead or Discipline Head. Maintain professional and academic currency through scholarship, research, professional development, industry or professional practice engagement and participation in relevant conferences and seminars. Collaborate with academic colleagues across Torrens Global Education to support continuous improvement, innovation and best practice in teaching and learning, while complying with relevant academic, regulatory and organisational requirements. Who you are An experienced academic or professional practitioner in Counselling, Psychotherapy or a closely related discipline, with significant knowledge of the subject area and a broad disciplinary background. You hold a PhD or equivalent qualification, or can demonstrate substantial educational leadership and relevant academic experience. Applicants who are currently, or eligible to be registered with the Australian Counselling Association (ACA) will be highly regarded. You have experience in higher education, with a sound understanding of current scholarship and professional practice in your discipline. You are experienced in delivering engaging student-centred learning across online, blended, face-to-face or practical learning environments. You can design or contribute to curriculum and assessment development, provide constructive feedback, and support students from diverse cultures, backgrounds and learning needs. You are a confident communicator and collaborative academic who is committed to continuous professional development, academic quality, innovation and student success. You are confident using learning technologies and understand relevant requirements, including TEQSA, , the Higher Education Standards Framework, ESOS and the National Code. To read more about the role please click here . This is a full-time, permanent, fully remote position that can be based in any of our four campuses. Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer :   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from: Study free in a course/degree related to your position Access to internal opportunities - be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation A purpose-driven workplace that values community, collaboration and innovation Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog. We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31370 Applications for this role will close on 2 December 2026 If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/QLD-Remote/Associate-Professor--Research---Training---Open-_R31174-2": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Research & Training)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-11\nFull time\n\nWho we are? At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do . What’s the job?   The Associate Professor in Research and Training provides academic leadership in research and research training, contributing to the University’s research profile, HDR experience and academic capability. The role is expected to demonstrate sustained excellence and leadership across at least two academic pillars, with Research and Innovation or Learning, Teaching and Scholarship forming one of those areas. As a member of the Professoriate, you will act as a role model and ambassador for Torrens University Australia, make a sustained contribution across the relevant discipline and vertical, and support the University to deliver its strategic objectives.    Principle accountabilities: Lead and contribute to high-quality research and research training, maintaining research integrity and compliance with relevant regulatory and institutional requirements. Attract, supervise and support HDR students, including as a Principal Supervisor, and contribute to the supervisor community of practice. Lead or co-lead research projects, funding submissions, research partnerships and high-quality research outputs that strengthen impact and influence. Mentor Early and Mid-Career Researchers, develop research teams and build capability across Research Centres and Verticals. Contribute to teaching, learning, scholarship, course and assessment quality, academic standards and continuous improvement, as appropriate to the appointment pathway. Build productive relationships with industry, government, professional bodies and the wider community to advance research, professional practice and external engagement. Provide academic leadership through collaboration, committees, communities of practice, governance and participation in the broader life of the University. Lead and promote a culture of innovation, collaboration, inclusion and high performance, while supporting the development of more junior academic staff. To read more about the role please click here to View job description This is a permanent full-time position, with the location able to be based remotely in South Australia. Who you are:  You are an established academic leader with a strong regional and national reputation in your discipline. You bring a record of research achievement, research training leadership and academic contribution, together with the ability to work collaboratively across a diverse university community. To be successful in this position you will have:  A PhD or equivalent qualification, with qualifications appropriate to the discipline and level of teaching. Substantial academic leadership experience in a tertiary education environment, including contribution to policy, governance, quality improvement or institutional initiatives. A strong record of research achievement, including external research income, high-quality research outputs and engagement with relevant national or international research communities. Experience attracting and supervising HDR students, developing research capability and mentoring Early and Mid-Career Researchers. Demonstrated ability to develop research partnerships and engage effectively with industry, government, professional bodies and other external stakeholders. Knowledge of research integrity, the Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research, human research ethics and relevant higher education regulatory standards. A commitment to high-quality learning and teaching, scholarship, student support and continuous improvement, where relevant to the appointment pathway. Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to work respectfully and effectively with people from diverse cultures and backgrounds.  Strong digital literacy, including the ability to use discipline-specific technologies and learning technologies as required. Why join us? Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer : We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from: Study free in a course/degree related to your position Access to internal opportunities - be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation A purpose-driven workplace that values community, collaboration and innovation Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the necessary information you need at each stage of this process to put your best self forward. Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. Applications close: 9 December 2026     Job reference:  R31174 If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Teaching-Fellow---Counselling--Psychotherapy---Mental-Health_R31501-1": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Counselling, Psychotherapy & Mental Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nPart time\n\nTeaching Fellow | School of Education and Community Wellbeing | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate. People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role As a Teaching Fellow, you’ll join the School of Education & Community Wellbeing within the Discipline of Counselling & Psychotherapy, where you’ll inspire and support students from counselling, psychotherapy and related disciplines. You'll deliver engaging learning experiences across subjects such as Interpersonal Communication, Person-Centred Practice, Theories of Counselling, Advanced Counselling Skills, Trauma-Informed Practice, and Working with Complex Clients. You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment.  We are open to part-time arrangements, with a minimum commitment of 0.6 FTE (3 days per week). Can be based in Sydney, Melbourne, Adelaide, Queensland, Western Australia or remotely.   What you'll bring  Master's degree in Counselling, Psychotherapy, Mental Health or a closely related discipline, or a partially completed PhD, is required. A completed PhD is highly regarded. Demonstrated experience teaching counselling, psychotherapy or a related discipline in a higher education setting and/or relevant professional experience, with the ability to bring contemporary industry knowledge and practice into learning environment. Current registration or professional membership with a relevant industry body, such as the Australian Counselling Association (ACA) or Psychotherapy and Counselling Federation of Australia (PACFA) or similar is highly regarded. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments in Higher Education Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities  A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning Relevant postgraduate qualifications (or working towards completion) How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different   There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes.  Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success.    Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact nikeey.silwal@torrens.edu.au for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Teaching-Fellow---Community-Services_R31498-1": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Community Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nTeaching Fellow | School of Education and Community Wellbeing | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate. People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role  As a Teaching Fellow, you'll join the School of Education and Community Wellbeing, where you'll inspire and support the next generation of community services professionals. You'll teach across the Bachelor of Community Services, delivering and engaging learning experiences in various community services related subjects.  You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. Full-time permanent position located at Flinders Campus in Melbourne. What you'll bring Master's degree in Community Services, Social Work, Welfare Work, or a closely related discipline; a PhD (completed or in progress) is highly regarded. Current registration or membership with Community Work Australia (CWA, formerly ACWA) or the Australian Association of Social Workers (AASW) is highly desirable. Demonstrated contemporary professional experience in the community services and social work sector, with expertise in one or more areas such as case management, mental health, family and child protection, homelessness and housing, youth services, or related fields. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments in Higher Education Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning Relevant postgraduate qualifications (or working towards completion) How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes.  Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success.    Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact nikeey.silwal@torrens.edu.au for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Teaching-Fellow---Education---Academic-Practice_R31496": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Education & Academic Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nEducation & Academic Practice Teaching Fellow | School of Education and Community Wellbeing | Full-time | Torrens University Australia   Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate. People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role Teaching Fellow – Education and Academic Practice As a Teaching Fellow, you’ll join the School of Education and Community Wellbeing, inspiring and supporting postgraduate students across our Education and Academic Practice portfolio. You’ll contribute to high-quality teaching and learning across Postgraduate Initial Teacher Education and specialised Education and Academic Practice programs, supporting student engagement, academic achievement and success. You’ll foster inclusive, supportive and engaging learning environments that encourage critical thinking, professional growth and lifelong learning. Desirable areas of specialisation include Inclusive Education, Leadership and Innovation, and Inclusive Literacies, Educational with a strong commitment to social justice, equity and inclusion across all areas of teaching practice.  With social justice, inclusion and meaningful change at the heart of our teaching philosophy, you’ll empower educators and professionals to challenge existing practices, embrace diversity, advocate for equity and drive positive change across educational and professional contexts. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. This is a full-time permanent position located at either Surry Hills Sydney, or Flinders Street, Melbourne Campuses. What you'll bring A Teaching qualification in either Early Childhood, Primary or Secondary Education or qualification in Education, Inclusive Education, Educational Leadership or a closely related discipline. A PhD (completed or in progress) is highly regarded. Demonstrated experience teaching in higher education, particularly within postgraduate Education and Academic Practice programs, with a strong commitment to student engagement, inclusive teaching practices and supporting student success. Demonstrated contemporary professional and/or academic experience in the education sector, with expertise in one or more areas such as Inclusive Education, Educational Leadership and Innovation, Inclusive Literacies, Neurodiversity, Social Justice, Educational Research, Academic Practice, Advocacy or Educational Change. A strong commitment to equity, inclusion and driving meaningful change in educational and professional contexts is highly desirable. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments in Higher Education Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes. Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success.    Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact nikeey.silwal@torrens.edu.au  for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Teaching-Fellow---Business_R31502-1": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nTeaching Fellow | School of Business | Full-time | Torrens University Australia   Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate. People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role  As a Teaching Fellow, you’ll join the School of Business to deliver engaging learning experiences across our Diploma, Bachelor’s and Master’s programs.  This is a full-time, permanent opportunity, with four Teaching Fellow positions available—one in each of Brisbane, Sydney, Melbourne and Adelaide. The subjects you teach will depend on your location: Adelaide: Understanding Self and Others   Brisbane, Sydney and Melbourne: Business Environment and Business Communications In this role, you’ll deliver engaging and interactive learning experiences that develop students’ self-awareness, communication, collaboration and professional skills.   You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centered around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. What you'll bring PhD (completed or in progress) is highly preferred. Demonstrated expertise in one or more core business disciplines, such as Accounting, Finance, Marketing, Management, Strategy or Economics, together with strong digital and analytical capabilities, including the application of AI and technology-enabled decision-making. Current industry practice with the ability to integrate contemporary business, responsible and sustainable business principles (including ethics, ESG, and governance), and best-practice learning and teaching approaches into the student experience. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments in Higher Education Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning Relevant postgraduate qualifications (or working towards completion) How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes.  Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success.    Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
