    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Teaching-Fellow---Foundation-Science_R31504": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Foundation Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nFoundation Science Teaching Fellow | School of Health Science and Clinical Practice | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate.    People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role As a Teaching Fellow, you’ll join the School of Health Science and Clinical Practice, inspiring and supporting the next generation of health professionals. You’ll teach across our Diploma, Bachelor’s and Master’s Health Science programs, with a focus on Foundation Sciences, including Anatomy and Physiology, Healthcare in the Digital World, Evidence-Based Practice, Critical Literature Review, Pathophysiology and Clinical Assessment. You’ll also contribute to curriculum development, subject review and continuous improvement across the Health Science programs. This includes designing contemporary learning activities, developing innovative assessment approaches and ensuring curriculum remains relevant, inclusive and aligned with student and industry needs. Contribute to curriculum development: Support the design, review and continuous improvement of subjects, learning resources and curriculum activities. Innovate in assessment: Design authentic, inclusive and engaging assessment activities that support learning, demonstrate student capability and promote employability. Engage in scholarship: Contribute to scholarship of teaching and learning by evaluating teaching practices, sharing insights and applying evidence to improve student outcomes.   You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details    We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. This is a full-time, permanent position based at the Wakefield Campus in Adelaide. What you'll bring MSc, PhD, or equivalent qualification in a relevant discipline. A relevant postgraduate qualification, such as master's degree, PhD or equivalent, in health sciences, healthcare, education or a related discipline. Relevant academic, teaching, research or professional experience in health sciences, healthcare, biomedical science, allied health, nursing, public health or a related discipline, with the ability to apply contemporary knowledge to teaching and student learning. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, explain a concept relevant to your discipline in 5 minutes through activity-based learning. We would like to understand your facilitation style, impact and capability.     Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes. Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success. Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Teaching-Fellow---Nutrition_R31503-1": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Nutrition",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nNutrition Teaching Fellow | School of Health Science and Clinical Practice | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate.    People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role As a Teaching Fellow (Nutrition), you’ll join the School of Health Science and Clinical Practice, delivering engaging learning experiences across the Diploma and Bachelor of Health Science programs. You’ll focus on subjects including Health Education and Communication, Food Science, Systems and Policy, Diet and Disease, and Public Health Nutrition.   You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details    We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. This is a full-time, permanent position based at the Wakefield Campus in Adelaide. What you'll bring Postgraduate qualification in Nutrition (Master's degree or higher); a PhD (completed or in progress) is highly regarded. Current membership with a relevant professional association, together with contemporary professional experience in the nutrition field and the ability to maintain active industry engagement alongside the role. Demonstrated experience in the healthcare sector, with the ability to apply industry knowledge to teaching and student learning. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning Relevant postgraduate qualifications (or working towards completion) How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes.  Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success. Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Dean----School-of-Health-Sciences---Clinical-Practice_R31492-1": {
      "title": "Dean -  School of Health Sciences & Clinical Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nWho we are:   At Torrens University Australia , making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.    A progressive university, we ground our studies in industry. Expert academics bring their insights into the classroom, with a range of assessment types that aim to be authentic and informed by industry needs. Bridging the gap between study and work, our educators prepare students for career success and connect them with future employers. Building relevant skills, experience and networks from day one, students don’t just learn about their industry, they live it.    What’s the job?   As Dean of the School of Health Sciences & Clinical Practice , you will be the senior academic and operational leader of the School, responsible for driving academic excellence, student success, industry engagement, innovation, growth and operational performance across its portfolio. Reporting to the Provost and Deputy Vice Chancellor Academic, you will lead the School in alignment with the University’s strategic direction, objectives and key performance indicators. You will oversee learning and teaching, academic quality, curriculum innovation, student experience, workforce capability, partnerships, financial sustainability and growth. You will lead a high-performing, industry-connected and student-centred School that delivers outstanding educational outcomes through innovative pedagogy, digitally enabled learning, authentic assessment and contemporary workforce-aligned curriculum. This is an exciting opportunity to help shape the future of higher education at Torrens University Australia. As the higher education ecosystem continues to evolve, you will be at the forefront of new and innovative approaches to teaching and learning. You will have the opportunity to build on the School’s existing identity, contribute to its continued growth and help shape its next chapter. This is a role for someone who is open to new ideas, embraces innovation and is excited to guide meaningful development and change.   Principle accountabilities (but not limited to): Strategic Leadership and Academic Quality Learning, Teaching and Curriculum Innovation Student Success and Experience Industry Engagement and External Partnerships Financial and Operational Leadership  Research, Scholarship and Innovation  People Leadership and Organisational Capability  Who you are - Criteria: 1. An experienced senior academic leader with a strong record in higher education or a multi-sector education environment, including responsibility for academic delivery, quality, student outcomes and operational performance. 2. You hold an earned doctorate and have academic standing appropriate for appointment at Professorial level, with demonstrated credibility in learning and teaching, academic governance and curriculum innovation. 3. You have a strong understanding of the Australian higher education regulatory environment, including TEQSA, the Higher Education Standards Framework, ESOS obligations and relevant professional accreditation requirements. 4. You have experience leading online, digitally enabled and multi-campus education, with a strong understanding of contemporary pedagogy, workforce-aligned curriculum and integrated higher education and vocational education pathways. 5. You bring experience managing complex academic operations, budgets, workforce planning, organisational change and industry partnerships that support employability and student outcomes. 6. You are an inspirational, inclusive and collaborative leader with strong communication, influencing and stakeholder engagement skills, a commitment to equity and inclusion, and a clear focus on student success and institutional impact. 7. Relevant qualifications or experience in health sciences, clinical practice or a related discipline would be highly regarded. Please submit your resume and a cover letter addressing the seven criteria outlined above. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent full-time position based at one of our Campus locations in Brisbane, Sydney, Melbourne and Adelaide.  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we are Australia's fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country's most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you will find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. Hiring process   Please submit your resume and a cover letter addressing the seven criteria outlined above. We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31492 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 9th December 2026. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    }
  },
